vers/laravel-queues-at-scale.svg" style="text-align:left;padding:0"><div class="th"><img src="<?= asset_url('images/covers/laravel-queues-at-scale.svg') ?>" alt=""></div><div class="mt2"><b>laravel-queues-at-scale.svg</b></div></button><button type="button" class="mi2" data-img="images/covers/saas-billing-basics.svg" style="text-align:left;padding:0"><div class="th"><img src="<?= asset_url('images/covers/saas-billing-basics.svg') ?>" alt=""></div><div class="mt2"><b>saas-billing-basics.svg</b></div></button><button type="button" class="mi2" data-img="images/chatrox-mobile.svg" style="text-align:left;padding:0"><div class="th"><img src="<?= asset_url('images/chatrox-mobile.svg') ?>" alt=""></div><div class="mt2"><b>chatrox-mobile.svg</b></div></button></div></div></div>
<script>window.ED_INIT={"blocks": [{"type": "lead", "t": "Multi-tenancy is the backbone of almost every B2B SaaS product: one codebase, one deployment, many customers, each of whom must feel like the system was built only for them. Laravel is an excellent fit for this, but the framework does not make the hard decisions for you."}, {"type": "p", "t": "We will cover what \u201ctenant\u201d actually means in your domain, how to identify the current tenant on every request, the three common database strategies and when each makes sense, and how to scope Eloquent queries so data never leaks."}, {"type": "h2", "t": "What Multi-Tenancy Means (and What It Doesn\u2019t)", "id": "what-is-multi-tenancy"}, {"type": "ul", "t": "**Tenant**: the organisation boundary (who owns the data).\n**User**: a person who logs in; may belong to one or several tenants.\n**Role / permission**: what that user may do within the current tenant."}, {"type": "callout", "k": "note", "title": "Note", "t": "If a user can belong to more than one tenant, model it as a `tenant_user` pivot with the role on the pivot, not a single `tenant_id` on the users table."}, {"type": "h2", "t": "Choosing a Database Strategy", "id": "choosing-a-database-strategy"}, {"type": "table", "head": "Strategy | Isolation | Ops complexity | Best for", "t": "**Single database, `tenant_id` column** | Logical (application-enforced) | Low | Most early-stage SaaS\n**Schema per tenant** (PostgreSQL) | Strong logical | Medium | Moderate tenant counts\n**Database per tenant** | Physical | High | Enterprise or regulated customers"}, {"type": "h3", "t": "Single database with a tenant_id column", "id": "single-database"}, {"type": "code", "lang": "php", "file": "database/migrations/create_invoices_table.php", "t": "Schema::create('invoices', function (Blueprint $table) {\n    $table->id();\n    $table->foreignId('tenant_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();\n    $table->string('number');\n    $table->decimal('total', 12, 2);\n    $table->timestamps();\n    $table->unique(['tenant_id', 'number']);\n});"}, {"type": "pull", "t": "Pick the simplest isolation model your customers will accept, and make the upgrade path to stronger isolation cheap."}, {"type": "h2", "t": "Scoping Queries So Data Never Leaks", "id": "scoping-queries"}, {"type": "steps", "t": "Create a global scope | Add `where tenant_id = ?` to every query on tenant-owned models.\nFill tenant_id on create | Set the column automatically in the `creating` event.\nWrap it in a trait | Every tenant-owned model uses `BelongsToTenant`, nothing else."}, {"type": "take", "title": "Key takeaway", "t": "Make isolation the default. A global scope plus a creating hook means a developer has to go out of their way to break tenancy."}, {"type": "mcta", "title": "Planning a multi-tenant SaaS?", "t": "Get a second opinion on your architecture before the database design is locked in.", "btn": "Book a free consultation \u2192", "url": "/contact"}, {"type": "img", "src": "images/banners/multi-tenant-crm.svg", "alt": "Diagram placeholder: tenant onboarding flow", "cap": "Placeholder figure: a typical onboarding pipeline (signup \u2192 tenant record \u2192 database \u2192 migrations \u2192 seed \u2192 invite)."}, {"type": "quote", "t": "Treat every cross-tenant data leak as a security incident, not a bug. Your customers will."}, {"type": "faq", "title": "Frequently Asked Questions", "t": "Which database strategy is best for a new Laravel SaaS? | For most new products, a single database with a tenant_id column is the simplest and cheapest to run.\nDo global scopes protect raw DB queries? | No. Global scopes only apply to Eloquent queries. Raw DB::table() and DB::select() calls need explicit tenant filters."}]};</script>
